Synthax : #TYPE;DBID;FILENAME;SIZE(optional);ORIENTATION(optional)
Possible types : ship ; aircraft ; vehicle ; facility ; submarine ; weapon ; satellite ; personnel</value></data>
  <data name="Button16.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button19.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button9.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button15.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button28.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="TB_Structure.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>This is a runtime global modification of icons.
The icons override is performed with 2 association files for each database type :
Associations_DB3000.csv and Associations_CWDB.csv (click on "open folder" to find them)
All custom icons must be placed in the "Custom" folder. Image must be .png, white (supports transparency), should not exceed 128px in size and be squared and ideally multiples of 2.

It is therefore required to change one of the file directly in a text editor, save the modifications and then either restart Command or click on the "reload" button.

The icon priority follows this order from highest to lowest : 1-Scenario unit custom icon 2-DBID custom icon 3- Type custom icon 4-Default command icon.</value></data>
  <data name="Button13.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button5.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button27.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button6.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button24.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button22.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button18.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="Button14.BackgroundImage" mimetype="application/x-microsoft.net.object.binary.base64"><value></value></data><data name="TB_Examples.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Example 1 :
#aircraft;2846;Drone.png;40;rot
Replaces aircraft DBID 2846 default icon to Drone.png, but also increases its size (from 20px to 40px)
We also specify that the icon will be rotated according to its orientation (rot).

Example 2 :
#submarine;92;Whale.png
Replaces submarine DBID 92 (a whale) from the default icon to the one specified. None of the optional argument were filled, the icon will be 20px and won't rotate.

Example 3 :
#ship;*;Ships.png
Replaces ALL ships icon to the one specified, note that DBID-specific override take precedence over type-specific ones.</value></data>
